        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "## Narrative",
          "",
          "An attacker who controls a computer can collect the credentials of other accounts that logged on to it. With these credentials, the attacker moves on to the next computer, collects credentials again, and continues. Each hop can use a different account, and each hop happens after the previous one.",
          "",
          "Scenario 2 counted every computer that a beachhead reaches within two hops, regardless of time. An attacker can only follow a path whose hops happen in the right order. This analysis follows such time-respecting paths: it starts from the confirmed compromises, checks where the victims connect to next, and which accounts they use. It then searches the full cyber graph for computers that relay an authentication from one account to another within the same hour.",
          "",
          "**Scope:** Steps 1 to 4 start from the confirmed red team events. Step 5 searches the full graph for chains of NTLM network logons, the logon pattern of the confirmed pivot in Scenario 2."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
