        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "### Before You Start",
          "",
          "One authentication event in the `AUTH` table becomes two edges in the cyber graph:",
          "",
          "- `auth_src_authenticated` links the account to the source computer. It carries the authentication details, such as `auth_type`, `logon_type`, and `success_failure`.",
          "- `auth_connected` links the source computer to the destination computer. It carries the red team flag `redteam`.",
          "",
          "Both edges share the key `id` of the event. The condition `a.id = h.id` in the pattern `(u IS user_domain) -[a IS auth_src_authenticated]-> (s IS computer) -[h IS auth_connected]-> (v IS computer)` joins them back into one hop: account `u` authenticates from `s` to `v`. A chain joins two such hops at the middle computer and requires the second hop to start after the first one. A variable-length pattern such as `->{1,2}` cannot compare the times of its hops, so the queries spell out each hop."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "## Analysis Flow",
          "",
          "### Overview",
          "",
          "1. **Chain Check in the Ground Truth** - check whether a labeled victim ever became the source of a later labeled compromise.",
          "2. **Onward Hops from Confirmed Victims** - find the computers that each victim connects to within one hour after its compromise, with the same or another account.",
          "3. **Credential Origin** - check whether the accounts used for the onward hops logged on to the victim before the compromise. Step 3a counts the onward targets that are new for the victim.",
          "4. **Time-Respecting Reach** - summarize the onward hops per staging host.",
          "5. **Chain Generalization** - find computers that relay an NTLM network logon from one account to another within the same hour, and check where the labeled computers rank.",
          "6. **Structural Ranking** - rank the computers at the end of the chains with PageRank."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "### Step 1: Chain Check in the Ground Truth",
          "",
          "The red team events record each compromise as a hop from a staging host to a victim. Did a victim ever become the source of a later labeled compromise? The query matches two consecutive `compromised` edges in the ground-truth graph and counts, per middle computer, the pairs in which the second hop happens after the first.",
          "",
          "If the query returns no rows, every labeled compromise starts at a staging host, and the labels contain no chains. Any onward movement from a victim then exists only in the unlabeled events, which Steps 2 to 4 examine."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%sql",
          "",
          "SELECT",
          "  middle_computer,",
          "  COUNT(*)                                              AS hop_pairs,",
          "  COUNT(CASE WHEN second_time > first_time THEN 1 END)  AS time_ordered_chains,",
          "  COUNT(DISTINCT staging_host)                          AS staging_hosts_in,",
          "  COUNT(DISTINCT next_victim)                           AS victims_out",
          "FROM",
          "  GRAPH_TABLE (",
          "    lanl_ground_truth_graph",
          "    MATCH",
          "      (s IS computer) -[r1 IS compromised]-> (v IS computer) -[r2 IS compromised]-> (w IS computer)",
          "    COLUMNS (",
          "      s.computer AS staging_host,",
          "      v.computer AS middle_computer,",
          "      w.computer AS next_victim,",
          "      r1.time    AS first_time,",
          "      r2.time    AS second_time",
          "    )",
          "  )",
          "GROUP BY",
          "  middle_computer",
          "ORDER BY",
          "  time_ordered_chains DESC,",
          "  hop_pairs DESC",
          "FETCH APPROX FIRST 100 ROWS ONLY;"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "table",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : false,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "**Result:** the query returns no rows. Every labeled compromise starts at one of the four staging hosts, and no victim became the source of a later labeled compromise. Any onward movement from the victims exists only in the unlabeled events."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "### Step 2: Onward Hops from Confirmed Victims",
          "",
          "Which computers does a victim connect to within one hour after its compromise, and with which accounts? The query starts from each confirmed red team hop into a victim and follows the victim's next authentication to another computer. It ignores connections back to the staging host and authentications on the victim itself.",
          "",
          "The result separates the onward hops by account:",
          "",
          "- `next_computers_same_account` counts the computers reached with the account of the confirmed hop.",
          "- `next_computers_other_account` counts the computers reached with another account, the shape of credential hopping.",
          "",
          "Like Scenario 1, the query excludes `ANONYMOUS LOGON`, `NETWORK SERVICE`, and machine accounts from the onward hops. `min_gap_seconds` shows the shortest time between a confirmed hop and an onward hop."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%sql",
          "",
          "SELECT",
          "  victim,",
          "  COUNT(DISTINCT compromise_id)                                               AS confirmed_hops_in,",
          "  COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN account_out = account_in THEN next_computer END)   AS next_computers_same_account,",
          "  COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN account_out <> account_in THEN next_computer END)  AS next_computers_other_account,",
          "  COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN account_out <> account_in THEN account_out END)    AS other_accounts_out,",
          "  MIN(hop_out_time - hop_in_time)                                             AS min_gap_seconds",
          "FROM",
          "  GRAPH_TABLE (",
          "    lanl_cyber_graph",
          "    MATCH",
          "      (u1 IS user_domain) -[a1 IS auth_src_authenticated]-> (s IS computer)",
          "        -[h1 IS auth_connected]-> (v IS computer)",
          "        -[h2 IS auth_connected]-> (w IS computer),",
          "      (u2 IS user_domain) -[a2 IS auth_src_authenticated]-> (v)",
          "    WHERE",
          "      h1.redteam = 1                           -- confirmed red team hop into the victim",
          "      AND a1.id = h1.id                        -- a1 and h1 come from the same AUTH event",
          "      AND a2.id = h2.id                        -- a2 and h2 come from the same AUTH event",
          "      AND h2.time > h1.time                    -- the onward hop starts after the compromise ...",
          "      AND h2.time <= h1.time + 3600            -- ... and within one hour",
          "      AND w.computer <> s.computer             -- ignore connections back to the staging host",
          "      AND w.computer <> v.computer             -- ignore local authentications on the victim",
          "      AND u2.user_domain NOT LIKE 'ANONYMOUS LOGON@%'",
          "      AND u2.user_domain NOT LIKE 'NETWORK SERVICE@%'",
          "      AND u2.user_domain NOT LIKE '%$@%'       -- machine/computer accounts, not human identities",
          "    COLUMNS (",
          "      v.computer     AS victim,",
          "      h1.id          AS compromise_id,",
          "      h1.time        AS hop_in_time,",
          "      u1.user_domain AS account_in,",
          "      h2.time        AS hop_out_time,",
          "      u2.user_domain AS account_out,",
          "      w.computer     AS next_computer",
          "    )",
          "  )",
          "GROUP BY",
          "  victim",
          "ORDER BY",
          "  next_computers_other_account DESC,",
          "  next_computers_same_account DESC",
          "FETCH APPROX FIRST 100 ROWS ONLY;"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "table",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : false,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "**Result:** all 100 victims in the result connect onward with another account than the one of the confirmed hop, and only 25 of them also with the same account. 38 of them make an onward hop within one minute after a confirmed hop. Two victims stand out:",
          "",
          "- `C754` reaches 92 computers with a single other account within an hour after its compromise.",
          "- `C1567` uses 51 other accounts for its onward hops."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "### Step 3: Credential Origin",
          "",
          "Where do the accounts of the onward hops come from? A harvested credential belongs to an account that logged on to the victim, so the query checks the logons on the victim (`auth_dst_authenticated` edges) before the account was used from it. `account_origin` classifies each victim-account pair:",
          "",
          "- `RESIDENT`: the account logged on to the victim before the compromise. Its credentials were on the victim, where the attacker could collect them.",
          "- `ARRIVED_AFTER_COMPROMISE`: the account first logged on to the victim after the compromise. The credentials came with the attacker.",
          "- `NO_LOGON_ON_VICTIM`: the account never logged on to the victim before it was used from it."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%sql",
          "",
          "WITH onward AS (",
          "  SELECT",
          "    victim,",
          "    account_out,",
          "    MIN(hop_in_time)              AS compromise_time,",
          "    MIN(hop_out_time)             AS first_hop_out_time,",
          "    COUNT(DISTINCT next_computer) AS next_computers",
          "  FROM",
          "    GRAPH_TABLE (",
          "      lanl_cyber_graph",
          "      MATCH",
          "        (u1 IS user_domain) -[a1 IS auth_src_authenticated]-> (s IS computer)",
          "          -[h1 IS auth_connected]-> (v IS computer)",
          "          -[h2 IS auth_connected]-> (w IS computer),",
          "        (u2 IS user_domain) -[a2 IS auth_src_authenticated]-> (v)",
          "      WHERE",
          "        h1.redteam = 1",
          "        AND a1.id = h1.id",
          "        AND a2.id = h2.id",
          "        AND h2.time > h1.time",
          "        AND h2.time <= h1.time + 3600",
          "        AND w.computer <> s.computer",
          "        AND w.computer <> v.computer",
          "        AND u2.user_domain <> u1.user_domain   -- onward hop with another account",
          "        AND u2.user_domain NOT LIKE 'ANONYMOUS LOGON@%'",
          "        AND u2.user_domain NOT LIKE 'NETWORK SERVICE@%'",
          "        AND u2.user_domain NOT LIKE '%$@%'",
          "      COLUMNS (",
          "        v.computer     AS victim,",
          "        h1.time        AS hop_in_time,",
          "        h2.time        AS hop_out_time,",
          "        u2.user_domain AS account_out,",
          "        w.computer     AS next_computer",
          "      )",
          "    )",
          "  GROUP BY",
          "    victim,",
          "    account_out",
          "),",
          "logons AS (",
          "  SELECT *",
          "  FROM",
          "    GRAPH_TABLE (",
          "      lanl_cyber_graph",
          "      MATCH (u IS user_domain) -[d IS auth_dst_authenticated]-> (c IS computer)",
          "      COLUMNS (",
          "        u.user_domain AS account,",
          "        c.computer    AS computer,",
          "        d.time        AS logon_time",
          "      )",
          "    )",
          ")",
          "SELECT",
          "  o.victim,",
          "  o.account_out,",
          "  o.next_computers,",
          "  CASE",
          "    WHEN COUNT(l.logon_time) = 0                THEN 'NO_LOGON_ON_VICTIM'",
          "    WHEN MIN(l.logon_time) < o.compromise_time  THEN 'RESIDENT'",
          "    ELSE 'ARRIVED_AFTER_COMPROMISE'",
          "  END                                                                 AS account_origin,",
          "  COUNT(CASE WHEN l.logon_time < o.compromise_time THEN 1 END)        AS logons_before_compromise,",
          "  o.compromise_time - MIN(l.logon_time)                               AS seconds_first_logon_to_compromise",
          "FROM",
          "  onward o",
          "  LEFT JOIN logons l",
          "    ON  l.account  = o.account_out",
          "    AND l.computer = o.victim",
          "    AND l.logon_time < o.first_hop_out_time   -- logons on the victim before the account was used from it",
          "GROUP BY",
          "  o.victim,",
          "  o.account_out,",
          "  o.next_computers,",
          "  o.compromise_time",
          "ORDER BY",
          "  o.next_computers DESC,",
          "  o.victim,",
          "  o.account_out",
          "FETCH APPROX FIRST 100 ROWS ONLY;"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "table",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : false,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "**Result:** of the 100 victim-account pairs in the result, 74 are `RESIDENT`. These accounts logged on to the victim long before the compromise, 6.6 days before it in the median case. Their credentials were on the victim, which fits credential harvesting. Resident accounts are also the normal users of a victim, so residence alone proves nothing. The signal is the combination: another account, used within an hour after a confirmed compromise.",
          "",
          "20 pairs are `ARRIVED_AFTER_COMPROMISE`, and 17 of them belong to `C1567`. These accounts first logged on to `C1567` between 13 minutes and one hour after its compromise and were then used from it. Their credentials came with the attacker. Several of these accounts appear in two domains, `DOM1` and `DOM9`, with the same user code. 6 pairs are `NO_LOGON_ON_VICTIM`."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "### Step 3a: New Targets After the Compromise",
          "",
          "Do the victims connect to computers they never used before? For each victim, the query compares the computers it connects to in the hour after its first compromise with the computers it connected to before. `new_next_computers_first_hour` counts the targets that the victim contacts for the first time in that hour, with any account. Normal activity mostly repeats known connections, so new targets right after a compromise point to onward movement.",
          "",
          "The workshop data starts on day 2, so for compromises early in the data the history before the compromise is short.",
          "",
          "> **Note:** this query groups all authentication events by source and destination computer and can run for about 13 minutes."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%sql",
          "",
          "WITH victims AS (",
          "  SELECT",
          "    victim,",
          "    MIN(compromise_time) AS first_compromise_time",
          "  FROM",
          "    GRAPH_TABLE (",
          "      lanl_ground_truth_graph",
          "      MATCH (s IS computer) -[r IS compromised]-> (v IS computer)",
          "      COLUMNS (",
          "        v.computer AS victim,",
          "        r.time     AS compromise_time",
          "      )",
          "    )",
          "  GROUP BY",
          "    victim",
          "),",
          "outbound AS (",
          "  SELECT",
          "    o.victim,",
          "    o.next_computer,",
          "    vi.first_compromise_time,",
          "    MIN(o.conn_time) AS first_seen,",
          "    MAX(CASE WHEN o.conn_time >= vi.first_compromise_time",
          "              AND o.conn_time <= vi.first_compromise_time + 3600 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS in_first_hour",
          "  FROM",
          "    GRAPH_TABLE (",
          "      lanl_cyber_graph",
          "      MATCH (v IS computer) -[p IS auth_connected]-> (w IS computer)",
          "      WHERE w.computer <> v.computer",
          "      COLUMNS (",
          "        v.computer AS victim,",
          "        w.computer AS next_computer,",
          "        p.time     AS conn_time",
          "      )",
          "    ) o",
          "    JOIN victims vi ON vi.victim = o.victim",
          "  GROUP BY",
          "    o.victim,",
          "    o.next_computer,",
          "    vi.first_compromise_time",
          ")",
          "SELECT",
          "  victim,",
          "  first_compromise_time,",
          "  COUNT(*)                                                               AS next_computers_overall,",
          "  COUNT(CASE WHEN first_seen < first_compromise_time THEN 1 END)         AS next_computers_before,",
          "  COUNT(CASE WHEN in_first_hour = 1 THEN 1 END)                          AS next_computers_first_hour,",
          "  COUNT(CASE WHEN in_first_hour = 1",
          "              AND first_seen >= first_compromise_time THEN 1 END)        AS new_next_computers_first_hour",
          "FROM",
          "  outbound",
          "GROUP BY",
          "  victim,",
          "  first_compromise_time",
          "ORDER BY",
          "  new_next_computers_first_hour DESC,",
          "  next_computers_first_hour DESC",
          "FETCH APPROX FIRST 100 ROWS ONLY;"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "table",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
