          "",
          "**Result:** all 100 victims in the result connect to other computers in the hour after their first compromise, 937 computers in total. Only 77 of them, about 8 percent, are new for the victim, and 25 victims contact any new computer at all. Most onward hops go to computers the victim already knew, so a new target alone is a weak signal. It marks a few victims strongly: `C1319` contacts 16 new computers out of 25, and `C2519` 15 out of 19."
        ],
